|term-group[match][designator][description]
  :status proposed

  A **MATCH** is the second mechanism by which a @{reference} reaches its @{referents}: instead of consulting a maintained @{binding}, a test is run at the moment of use. With @{binding} it forms the two connection mechanisms, and the classic vocabulary — **DESIGNATOR** and **DESCRIPTION** — derives from which mechanism a @{reference}'s connection actually uses, never from how it is spelled.

  |term[match      ] A connection from a reference to referents established by running a test at the moment of use: the referents are whatever, in the world's current population, passes the criteria the reference supplies.
    :avoid [search query] ; each names an activity or artifact, not the connection established
    |invariants
      - Nothing is minted and nothing is maintained; the answer may differ whenever the population differs
      - Fails through the world's motion: the same criteria, run later, quietly pick out something else — detectable only if the reference carries something to check against
  |term[designator ] A reference (or component of one) that reaches its referent through a @{binding} on its name.
  |term[description] A reference (or component of one) that reaches its referents by match.

  |discussion
    - Designator/description follows the connection, never the spelling: one written form is a designator where maintainers police the binding, and a description over a population nobody polices. Kind follows maintenance.
    - The two mechanisms' complementary failure modes — a binding fails through its maintenance, a match through the world's motion — drive all the later machinery.
    - A binding's name, viewed as a reference (per @{binding}'s intro), is the degenerate designator; a match whose test is "bytes equal exactly this content" (a hash) is match at its most designator-like — the two mechanisms meet at the corners without merging.

  |examples
    |          Example           |          The test              |
    |----------------------------|--------------------------------|
    | A glob                     | Name-pattern over what's present |
    | "The resident aged 47"     | Property over occupants        |
    | A WHERE clause             | Predicate over rows            |
    | A content hash             | Bytes equal                    |
    | A full-text search         | Contains the phrase            |

  |working-notes
    - Exhaustiveness — every addressing form examined decomposes into bindings consulted and matches run (positional index = match on the current ordering; hash = match on content; forwarding pointer = a binding at the old endpoint) — is held provisionally with its refutation stated: a mechanism that is neither reorganizes this layer.
    - Open: whether "population" (what a match tests against) needs its own definition or is carried by @{scope} once resolution is in hand.
